"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527361594","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111805#issuecomment-3527361594","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111805","id":3527361594,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SP0Q6","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T11:25:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T11:25:35Z","body":"I got a bit **confused** by this feature. I thought it would link to the code inside github at first.\r\nI get that opening the local file is a very useful feature for debugging in dev. \r\nBut it might be confusing for people that are using the engine.\r\n\r\n**Here's what happen:** When opening Godot Editor with no dev environment, I clicked the error link, but then it just opened vscode with an empty new file named after the cpp file that gave the error.\r\n\r\nThis could confuse the engine users to think this is a bug.\r\n\r\nSo it might be a good idea to link to github instead by default in the release version. \r\nMake it toggleable in the EditorSettings, or check if the file exists and go from there.\r\n\r\nUnless I'm missing something?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527361594/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527381287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111805#issuecomment-3527381287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111805","id":3527381287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SP5En","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T11:31:10Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T11:31:10Z","body":"> it just opened vscode with an empty new file named after the cpp file that gave the error.\r\n\r\nThis shouldn't be happening, it's supposed to open the file only if it exists.\r\n\r\n> So it might be a good idea to link to github instead by default in the release version.\r\n\r\nI can try that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527381287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3547108219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111805#issuecomment-3547108219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111805","id":3547108219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TbJN7","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T11:27:58Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T11:27:58Z","body":"> This shouldn't be happening, it's supposed to open the file only if it exists.\r\n\r\nJust for reference, here's a video.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b44b45f6-e05f-468b-8b10-b044be57d967\r\n\r\nIt only happens because I have vscode setup as the external text editor.\r\nBut I don't think it should be happening if it doesn't find the file.\r\n\r\n> > So it might be a good idea to link to github instead by default in the release version.\r\n> \r\n> I can try that.\r\n\r\nThat would be awesome. Even though I have Godot source here, I often prefer to go to github to browse the code if I'm just trying to understand something simple. It would be very helpful if it did so when the file is not present, or even with an editor setting toggle.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3547108219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]